# Managed by toolbox — see issue #366 (git over ssh re-prompts host-key
# verification). The ~/.ssh credential mount is read-only by design (a symlink
# that follows the host), so the Debian default StrictHostKeyChecking=ask +
# read-only ~/.ssh/known_hosts deadlocks: ssh prompts on first contact and then
# can't persist the accepted key. accept-new trusts host keys on first contact
# without prompting, still rejects CHANGED keys (anti-MITM), and writes them to
# a writable known_hosts on the persistent state mount so they survive
# `toolbox stop`. ~/.toolbox-state is the state mount target dir (always
# exists), so ssh creates the known_hosts file itself on first accept.
Host *
    StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new
    UserKnownHostsFile ~/.toolbox-state/known_hosts
